<title>SOUTH KOREA: Cheiljedang buys 35,000T U.S. soybean.</title>
<headline>Cheiljedang buys 35,000T U.S. soybean.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp bought 35,000 tonnes of U.S. No.2 soybean at a basis price over March futures on the Chicago Board of Trade, a company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The official said the company bought the soybeans from Japnese trading house Marubeni Corp with shipment slated for March 1-15 from the U.S. Gulf.</p>
<p>Arrival was set for the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>He said the purchase price was equivalent to around $300 per tonne FOB.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
